      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ios): replace the tab bar with a black overlay sidebar (web parity + dashboard)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe iPhone app's bottom tab bar caps root navigation at four tabs (Chat / Control / Agent / Settings), hides most destinations behind the Control hub, and diverges from both the iPad shell and the web Control UI. Sessions are not reachable in one gesture from anywhere, and the attention/overview signals the web sidebar carries (pending approvals, failing automations, thread stats) have no iPhone-native surface. Related asks: #105238 (fast in-chat session switching) and the Overview retirement direction from #104818.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMaintainer-directed redesign: converge every iPhone/iPad layout on one sidebar shell with the web sidebar's feature set, styled as a black overlay drawer.\n\n- **Tab bar removed.** `RootTabs` now always uses the sidebar shell; the phone `TabView`, Control hub, and phone-only chat-return plumbing are deleted (`RootTabsPhoneControlHub.swift`, `RootTabsPhoneChrome.swift`, `AppTab`).\n- **One toggle, top right.** Every root header shows a single trailing `line.3.horizontal` button (glass on iOS 26, bordered fallback on iOS 18); accessibility identifiers `RootTabs.Sidebar.Show`/`Hide` are unchanged.\n- **Black overlay drawer.** Slides from the leading edge at 86% width (max 340pt), full height under the status bar, continuous 28pt rounded trailing corners, 35% scrim with tap-to-dismiss and interactive drag-dismiss, spring animation with Reduce Motion fallbacks. Fixed palette mirrors the web Control UI dark tokens (`ui/src/styles/base.css`) in both appearances via `OpenClawSidebarPalette`.\n- **Web sidebar feature parity.** New Chat action, session search, inline recent-sessions list (pinned + recent, unread dots, active-run spinner, long-press rename/pin/fork/archive/delete via the existing `sessions.patch`/`sessions.create`/`sessions.delete` transport), flat Pages list echoing the web nav order, attention rows (pending approvals, failed/overdue cron), and a footer with gateway status + Settings. Session grouping reuses the shared `ChatSessionSidebarModel` from OpenClawChatUI (previously macOS-only, now public cross-platform).\n- **Dashboard absorption.** The web retired its Overview page and dissolved those features into sidebar attention + Threads tiles + Usage; the iOS Overview (`CommandCenterTab`) now carries them natively: Threads/Live/Unread/Tokens tiles, attention card, 31-day usage card with daily trend, all tapping through to their destinations. The parsed-but-dead `openclaw://dashboard` deep link now navigates to Overview.\n- Launch aliases (`--openclaw-initial-tab chat|talk|voice|control|agent|settings`) still map to destinations for UITests/fastlane compatibility.\n\n## User Impact\n\niPhone users get the full destination set (Overview, Workboard, Usage, Automations, Sessions, Activity, Skill Workshop, Agents, Instances, Files, Dreaming, Terminal, Docs, Settings) from one button, with their sessions and attention items one gesture away — same mental model as the web app. iPad keeps its persistent split sidebar in wide layouts, restyled to match.\n\n| Before (tab bar) | After (chat) | After (sidebar) | After (overview) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ![before](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr-ios-sidebar-20260719/before-chat.png) | ![after chat](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr-ios-sidebar-20260719/after-chat.png) | ![after sidebar](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr-ios-sidebar-20260719/after-sidebar-open.png) | ![after overview](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr-ios-sidebar-20260719/after-overview.png) |\n\nOld Control hub for reference: https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr-ios-sidebar-20260719/before-control.png\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm ios:gen` + `pnpm ios:build`: **BUILD SUCCEEDED** (iOS Simulator).\n- Focused unit tests green on iPhone 17 (iOS 26): `RootTabsPresentationTests`, `RootTabsSourceGuardTests`, `RootTabsSidebarRegressionTests`, `RootSidebarTypographyTests`, `SwiftUIRenderSmokeTests`, `LicenseDocumentLoaderTests`, `RuntimeLocalizationSourceGuardTests`.\n- `swift test --package-path apps/shared/OpenClawKit`: 1019 tests, 0 failures (macOS compile of shared model proven).\n- Snapshot UITests rewritten for the sidebar shell (same screenshot names); `build-for-testing` + smoke `testSidebarOverviewNavigation` passed on simulator.\n- `pnpm native:i18n:sync` + `pnpm apple:i18n:check` + `pnpm native:i18n:check` clean; new strings inventoried (human translations pending as advisories).\n- Screenshots above captured on iPhone 17 simulator in `--openclaw-screenshot-mode` (sanitized fixture data).\n- Known follow-ups: cron attention counts cap at 200 jobs; web sidebar's custom category groups and Coding/external-catalog sections are deliberately deferred.\n",
        "branch": "claude/ios-sidebar-redesign-5ee596",
